  "body": "## Change and scope\n\nFreestanding `#840`-style priced obstruction under [#1898](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1898) at `(b,a,x)=(38,2,2)`. Names the one-repeat companion of the partitioned `(2,6)` Hamilton layer at `Q=8`. Answers open question 1 of [#2851](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2851): do non-distinct (one-repeat) label layers inside a partitioned `Q=8` walk improve on distinct-label `R=92` at `(2,6)`?\n\n| Dual schedule | Covering pairs | Exact min R | Tariff floor (X\u22650) | Undercuts 436? | Beats distinct 92? |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|\n| Distinct-label `(2,6)` (#2851) | 3916416 | **92** | \u2265488 | no | \u2014 |\n| One-repeat long `(2,6)` (this) | **59996160** | **112** | **\u2265528** | **no** | **no** |\n\nEvery covering one-repeat dual has exact `R=112` (spectrum `{112}`). Only rank-4 longs cover, always with `\u03a3e=40` and `\u03c3` outside the long span (16 choices), so `R=2\u00b740+32=112`. Abstract tariff `38\u00b78+2\u00b7112=528>436`. Distinct-label floor `92` is not improved. Length-1 components are not restored. Rank`<4` longs are dual-scanned with `covering_rank_lt4=0`.\n\n**Scoped obstruction / priced alphabet; no new kappa.** Leave-alone through [#2860](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2860) / [#2858](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2858) / [#2851](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2851) / [#2846](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2846) was not reopened.\n\n## Result\n\nPackage: `research/independent-walks-onerepeat-8q/`.\nTip: `b07bc1e16752a1980c7dab098d6a4b98295d73c0`.\n\nExact: one-repeat min R **112** (tariff floor **528**); no undercut of 436; does not beat distinct 92.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/independent-walks-onerepeat-8q/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -O -B research/independent-walks-onerepeat-8q/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -B research/independent-walks-onerepeat-8q/independent.py\npython3.12 -I -B research/independent-walks-onerepeat-8q/test_package.py\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/independent-walks-onerepeat-8q\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n```text\nPASS_INDEPENDENT_WALKS_ONEREPEAT_8Q_OBSTRUCTION one_repeat_min_R=112 ... tariff_floor=528 ... answers_independent_walks_8q_oq1_onerepeat no_new_kappa\nPASS_INDEPENDENT_WALKS_ONEREPEAT_8Q covering=59996160 ... one_repeat_min_R=112 tariff_floor=528 ... no_new_kappa\nPASS_INDEPENDENT_WALKS_ONEREPEAT_8Q_PACKAGE_TESTS groups=6\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/independent-walks-onerepeat-8q outcome=completed\n```\n\nDefault verify is read-only. Admission uses `need()`; `-O` also passes.\n\n## Overlap and credit\n\nClosest prior: [#2851](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2851) (distinct partitioned Q=8), [#2858](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2858) (one-repeat `(3,5)`/`(4,4)`), [#2860](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2860) (two-repeat), [#2846](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2846), [#2779](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2779). Freestanding one-repeat layer on partitioned `(2,6)`; no competing open PR at refresh.\n\nCredit the mutable-source / #2851 / #2858 / #2860 / #2846 / #2779 / PR1898 lineage. Prepared by Wentao Li ([VictorLiwentao](https://github.com/VictorLiwentao), [@Is__Victor](https://x.com/Is__Victor)) with substantial AI assistance, under Apache-2.0.",
